# Keep the HPC scripts LF even when the repo is checked out on Windows.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is set here, so without this the next Windows checkout would rewrite these
# files with CRLF — and WinSCP transfers the WORKING TREE, so the HPC would receive scripts whose
# every line ends in a CR. Linux `/bin/sh` and `bash` then fail with `$'\r': command not found`,
# which is an obscure way to lose an array job. Julia and R sources are unaffected (both read CRLF
# fine) and are deliberately left alone.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.slurm text eol=lf
Dockerfile*  text eol=lf
